        <p>VIIS'S EVA SHAW, 83, LYTHOOES LANE, TIJiOR for PlANO.—Terrne on application.</p>
        <p>THE RURAL DISTRICT COUNCIL OF RUNCORN. PRIVATE STREET WORKS ACT, 1892. NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN, that the Rural District Council of Runcorn, being the Sanitary Authority for the Rural District of Runcorn, in the County of Chester, have, in pursuance of the Private Street Works Act, 1592, at a meeting held on the 24th day of September, 1912, by resolution approved of certain specifications, plans and sections, estimates and provisional apportionments, prepared by their Surveyor 'in respect of the following street : SMITH STREET And certain Passages in the Parish of WALTON INFERIOR in the said District, and that such resolution is in the following terms, that is to say : (a) That the Rural District Council of Runcorn, being the Sanitary Authority for the Rural District of Runcorn, level, pave, metal, flag, channel, and make good the following streets or parts of streets and passages, in the Parish of Walton Inferior, in the said District, under the provisions of the Private Street Works Act, 1892, viz. : Smith Street throughout its existing extent as measured in a south-westerly direction from its junction with Chester New Road to a point 71 feet from the said junction. Passage situate at the rear of houses numbered 1,3, 5, 7 and 9, Smith Street. Passage commencing at the south-western extremity of the Passage lastly herein-before described and extending to its junction with Taylor-street. , Passage situate at the rear of houses numbered 2,4, 6, 8 and 10, Smith Street. Passage situate at the rear of houses numbered 1,3, 5,7, 9, 11, 13, 15 and 17, Taylor Street. Passage situate at the rear of houses numbered 12 to 19, Eastford Road, and continuing in a westerly direction to its junction with East ford Road. Passage situate at the rear of houses numbered 1 to 9, Chester New Road, continuing in a northerly direction to its junction with Taylor Street. • Passage situate at the rear of houses numbered 2,4. 6,8, 10,12, 14, 16 and 18, Taylor Street. Passage situate at the rear of houses numbered 1 to 11, Eastford Road. Passage situate at the rear of houses numbered 1 to 14, Morley Road. (I 3 That the Specifications, Plans, Sections, Estimates, and Provisional Apportionments prepared and submitted by the Surveyor in respect of the said Streets or parts of streets and passages, be and are hereby approved. (o) That it be, and is, hereby ordered and declared that the expenses incurred in executing the aforesaid Private Street Works shall be payable by equal annual instalments extending over a period of ten years, with interest at the rate of £4 per centum per annum. (d) That application be made to the Local Govern- ment Board for their sanction to a loan for the required amount. AND NOTICE IS HEREBY FURTHER GIVEN, that the approved Specifications, Plans and Sections, Estimates and Provisional Apportionments (or copies thereof certified by the Surveyor)will he kept deposited at 71, High Street, Runcorn, the Office of the Rural District Council of Runcorn, and will be open to inspection at all reasonable times for a period of one month from the 12th day nf October,l9l2, during which period any owner of premises affected may in pursuance of Section 7 of the said Act, by written notice served on the said Council, object to the proposals of the said Council on any of the grounds in such section specified. Dated this 11th day of October' 1912. GEO. F. ASHTON. 71, High Street, Runcorn. Clerk to the Rural District Council of Runcorn.</p>
