      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1912-10-19_WidnesExaminer_art0030" n="art0030">
        <head>RUNCORN STILL LOSING.</head>
        <p>RUNCORN STILL LOSING.</p>
        <p>Rochdale were able to claim a victory at Irwell-lane. The home team played a fine game, and during the first half they had the greater share of the play, though the interval came with the score sheet blank. Rochdale were an improved side in the second half, but it was well on in the half before the first score came Watton being penalised for off-side, and Paddon placing a splendid goal from the half-way line. At length a nice bit of combination on the part of Rochdale carried the game into the Runcorn quarter, when Roman accepted a palpable forward pass before going over with the try which, however, was allowed. Paddon added the goal, and this 'completed the scoring. Result :—Rochdale Hornets, 2 goals and I try (7 points); Runcorn nil. Teams : Runcorn—Shaw, back • Whitfield, Hughes, Thornton, and Newell, three-quarter back ; Watton and Steel, half-back • Richsrdson, Niman, Massey, Peacock, 'Massey and Stevenson, forwards.</p>
        <p>Rochdale Hornets—Reade, back ; West, Robinson, Jones and Paddon, three-quarter backs ; Taylor and Prudence. half backs ; Woods, Fitzsimmon, Richardson Roman, Carter, and Slade forwards. Referee, H Ednaundson, Bradford.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1912-10-19_WidnesExaminer_art0031" n="art0031">
        <head>FRIENDLY MATCH.</head>
        <p>FRIENDLY MATCH.</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON " A " PILE UP POlNTS.—ikillth interest was shown in the first appeaiance for Warrington on Saturday, of Sidney Nicholas, the young half-back from South Wales, who appeared in the team to meet Salford St Bartholomews at Wilderspool.There was an attend- ance of quite 3,000 and a fine display was given by the home team against some very weak opposition. Nicholas was particularly clever at the base of the scrum and provided the backs with countless oppor- tunities. Dickenson scored in the first minute for Critchlev to goal, and by the interval Warrington had scored 25 points. In the second half they completely ran away from the Salford lads and added another 40 points, the final score being : Warrington" A "7 goals 17 tries (65 points) ; Salford St Bartholomews nil. The scorers were Nicholas 5 goal.. 3 tries, Clare 5 tries, Jordan 3 tries, Carter 2 tries, Dickenson 2 tries, Critchley 2 goals andpouglas and Cooper 1 try each.</p>
      </div>
