      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1912-10-19_WidnesExaminer_art0040" n="art0040">
        <head>CROSFIELD'S CLUB._</head>
        <p>CROSFIELD'S CLUB._</p>
        <p>The above club opened their season well last Saturday, beating Sale Moor by 4 goals to 2. This is all the more satisfactory seeing that Sale Moor beat their last week's opponents (Oldham) by 11 goals to nil and it speaks well for Crosfleld's considering that Sale Moor put out the same team again. The chief feature of the game was the great improve- ment on last year's form, which argurs well for the future. El C Bloomer played well at centre,scoring from a most difficult angle. He was well supported by B T Dixon and T A Dean as inside. H Sandy at centre-half excelled himself. A Mellor as goalkeeper was in excel- lent trim, saving remarkably well—as usual—in fact hia play has been noticed by other clubs, who have vainly tried to induce him to leave his own club. _ _</p>
        <p>The scorers were H C Bloomer 3, and TA Dean 1. To-day Crosflelo's are at home to Winnington Park and the team is as follows :—Goal, A Mellor ; backs, SV U Rench, E Paget ; half-backs, A Hodson, J Harrison (rapt). 3 Evans; forwards, A 1,5 thgoe,T Dean,H Sandy, H C Bloomer, B T Dixon.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1912-10-19_WidnesExaminer_art0041" n="art0041">
        <head>LATCHFORD CLUB.</head>
        <p>LATCHFORD CLUB.</p>
        <p>The First Elev-e-n—s-Coal—hWe Pll;;;Cl.Northern A last week but only the B team was sent and as might be expected they received a big thrashing by 3.1. Except 1 for the opening quarter of aq hour the game was rather I one-sided and Latchford bad things pretty much their own way, the forwards getting some shooting practice. The visiting centre worked hard but was badly supported by his other forwards. The goals for the home side I were scored by Banks (4), Pearson (3) Jones (2). 'The Second Eleven were playing on the excellent ground of the Carlton Club at Southport and won 4-0. It was a somewhat surprising result, the last 3 goals looming quite near the end of the game. Latchford scored once in the first half and had their work cut out to retain a lead, but fortunately the hacks were on their best behaviour. Near the finish Latchford put on great pressure and the Southport backs had a lively time- In spite of the stubborn resistance of the full backs and goal keeper (the latter in particular making several good saves) the ball was netted three times and the vititors won easily. Bruhl at full-hack for Latchford hit well and the half backs Gibbs, Bradshaw and Banks played very neatly. The goals were scored by Colton (1) Starkey (3). The First Eleven v St Helens at home this afternoon is :—Wright, goal ; Fletcher, Billington, backs ; Isherwood, Wilkinson, Knight, halves ; Dale, Pearson, Travis, Minards, Starkey, forwards. Referee, Mr C3bb. Bully-off 2.45 p.m. The Second Eleven at St Helens is :—Three full back, Eccles, Bruhl, Mull ; Gibbs, Bradshaw, T Banks, halves ; Leaver, Jones, Hackney. Banks, Colton. Referee, Mr DiYOD. Train from Bank Quay (Low Level) 1.54 p.m.</p>
      </div>
