        <p>F.</p>
        <p>Coming Events. The Rev. John Howarth, of Bolton, will deliver the ; aecond of his series of New Church lectures in the ; kasonic Ball, Bold-street, on Tuesday evening next, at . 7-45. The subject of his address will be " The Providence of God." "Bella Donna," performed by M. Alban B. Lirrpus' eompany, will be the great attraction at the Royal - Court Theatre next week. Every evening and - Thursday matinee. A. laymen's meeting of protest against the Welsh bisestablishment Bill will be held in the Parr Hall on Uonday evening. Mr R H Armitage will preside and the speakers will be the Right Hon. Lord Dynevor and 'LT W A Wheel, Llansamlet,Glamorgan (Member of the Steel Smelters' Trade Union). The town's meeting in support of the Criminal Law kclendment (White Slave Traffic) Bill will be held in The Parr Hall on Monday evening, The principal tPeaker will be Miss Thyrza Potts, M.A., of alanchester, and Miss Chamberlain, of Liverpool. Personal. The deepest sympathy has been expressed by all abalone of the community with Mr and Mrs J El I iliethurst, Briery Croft, on the sudden death of their tw°"Year-old son. t CORRUGATED SHEETS and Roofing Felt. Estimates rces---J. 8. GARLAND, Ironmonger, 51, Bridge at., p arrington.—Advt. Alleged Shortage of Magistrates. t Viscount Wolmer will ask the Chancellor of the a., 'icily of Lancaster on Monday whether his attention been called to the shortage of magietrates at the Warrington Petty Sessions, and whether it is intended I,° appoint any more justices of the peace for that . veuch. srown Council. There will be an additional meeting of the Council 20 Tuesday evening when, in addition to the ordinary ';'.esiness, the customary vote of thanks to the Mayor lor his services in the chair during the previous year, win be passed. The resolution is to be moved by Alderman Smethurst. The Picturedr3me. The pictures next week will be of the usual high j ,t3tandard and the chief films will be, Monday and -itiesday "The siege of Petersbu