      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1912-10-19_WidnesExaminer_art0143" n="art0143">
        <head>MR. ROOSEVELT.</head>
        <p>MR. ROOSEVELT.</p>
        <p>An attempt was made on Monday evening on the life of Mr. Roosevelt. The ex- President was leaving the Hotel Gilpatriek, Milwaukee. to address a political meeting, when he .was shot in the chest by a fanatic.</p>
        <p>The ex-President, though wounded, con- tinued his journey and addressed the gatheripg. Afterwards, he proceeded to the hospital', where the wound was examined, and found to be only superficial.</p>
      </div>
