        <p>UNITED KINGDOM ALLIANCE. At the annual meetings of the United Kingdom Alliance, which were held in Manchester on Monday, the president, Mr Leif Jones, M.P., said the council meeting was a noteworthy one, because he hoped it was the last before entering on what might be their final campaign on behalf of the adoption of local option by the people of the country. Mr Acland, Under-Secretary for Foreign Affairs, said they were under a moral obligation, before housing, and rating, and wages, to clear out of the way all those things which the House of Lords had prevented them from doing. • IDEAL BEALTII INSPECTOR. "MUST BE TEETOTALER AND NON-SMOKER." Dr. Francis Vacher, president of the North-Western centre of the Sanitary Inspectors' Association, in his , address to the members of the association at Manchester on Saturday night, said the ideal inspector for public health purposes must be a total abstainer and a non- smoker. As regards tobacco, its use was .nore or less injurious. It had a bad effect upon the heart and upon the vision. Smoking acted as a throat irritant, and, when there was a tendency to throat disease, other evils might follow.</p>
